laurel 2013: the USB gadget is served from a timer call (interrupt context, 1 ms) until bsd_init attaches ue0, not from a kernel thread: on the first UEFI boot (2026-11-01 02:28) the host asked GET_DESCRIPTOR for 30 s and got no answer because the boot hung after 'trust caches unavailable' and the service thread never ran (kernel_bootstrap_thread never blocked, or no timer interrupt). In the callback: no locks, spin delays, printf into the console ring only (console I/O with interrupts off panics on arm64). ud_thread prints the status lines and takes over at the attach. Self-check at STARTUP(LOCKDOWN) (right after the trust caches, on the panel): 'LAUREL USB: timer service: on, first tick after N us' or 'NO tick in 50 ms' + EL/DAIF/ISR/CNTV/ICC_*/GICD_CTLR/GICR state of the boot CPU (pe_fiq.c sweet_gic_state). pe_init_fiq also clears ICC_AP1R0_EL1 so no active priority left by the firmware blocks the PPIs/SGIs.
